# Strumming: Sixteenth-Note Funk (repertoire plan: st-strum-funk). An original 8-bar study on one
# chord, E9 (x76777): finger 2 on string 5 fret 7, finger 1 on string 4 fret 6, finger 3 laid flat
# across strings 3, 2 and 1 at fret 7. String 6 is muted by the tip of finger 2.
# The strumming hand never stops: four strokes in every beat, down on the beat and on the "and",
# up on the "e" and the "a". D and U strike the chord; X is the same stroke with the fretting
# fingers relaxed so the strings are muted (a dry scratch). Every X carries its direction.
# Two 2-bar patterns, each played twice:
#   A (bars 1-2, 3-4): chord on 1, &, e of 2, a of 2, & of 3, 4, a of 4 | 1, & of 2, a of 2,
#      e of 3, 4, & of 4
#   B (bars 5-6, 7-8): chord on 1, a of 1, & of 2, e of 3, a of 3, & of 4 | & of 1, 2, a of 2,
#      & of 3, 4, then scratches to the end of the bar
# Squeeze the chord only for the strokes that sound and let go at once, so every chord is short.
# The teacher's bass plays a plain E and its octave underneath.
title: Strumming: Sixteenth-Note Funk
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original strumming study in the funk style
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 6
tags: strumming, funk, sixteenth notes, muted strums, scratch, e9
tempo: 92
time: 4/4
key: E

track: Your strum
role: rhythm
[Pattern A]
| ^"Down on the beat, up on the e and a" "E9=x76777" s D X{up} D X{up} X{dn} U X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} D X{up} X{dn} U | D X{up} X{dn} X{up} X{dn} X{up} D U X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} D X{up} |
| D X{up} D X{up} X{dn} U X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} D X{up} X{dn} U | D X{up} X{dn} X{up} X{dn} X{up} D U X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} D X{up} |
[Pattern B]
| D X{up} X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} X{dn} U X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} | X{dn} X{up} D X{up} D X{up} X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} D X{up} X{dn} X{up} |
| D X{up} X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} X{dn} U X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} | X{dn} X{up} D X{up} D X{up} X{dn} U X{dn} X{up} D X{up} D X{up} X{dn} X{up} ||

